  "imagery": "Imagery is scarce and entirely functional. The only photograph is the hero specimen: a moody, low-key product shot of a monitor displaying a type specimen, set on a dark stone or concrete plinth. It is desaturated to near-monochrome, full-bleed, and unframed — no rounded corners, no drop shadow, no overlay. Everything else on the site is pure typography: no icons beyond thin line glyphs (play, cart), no illustrations, no decorative graphics. The visual language is the type itself, and the photograph exists only to prove the type looks as good in physical space as it does on screen.",
